id: hac-poex
title: Implement typed bounded media browse search and resolve
description: "Build the agent-native Home Assistant media discovery command surface with current WebSocket payloads, validated inputs, bounded result projections, exhaustive tests, documentation, live read-only proof, and release-safe delivery."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[6]: agents,implementation,media,search,typescript,websocket
created_at: "2026-07-25T22:32:44.658Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T23:07:24.756Z"
deadline: "2026-07-27T22:32:44.658Z"
assignee: codex-root
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Typed hassio media browse/search/resolve payloads match Home Assistant Core dev source and media player search remains compatible with local stable Core; Search query, scope, entity/source selectors, media content type, current media classes, count, and positive safe-integer limits validate before network I/O; TOON is default and TOON/JSON/compact JSON/YAML/table/markdown outputs retain stable documented envelopes; Focused, full, coverage, docstring, type, lint, duplication, file-size, ShellCheck, audit, Trivy, package, setup wizard, PM, changelog, and non-publishing release gates pass"
definition_of_ready: "Feature hac-ln1v and approved plan hac-h3uj capture duplicate-safe lineage, research, privacy, and compatibility constraints"
goal: complete-home-assistant-api-coverage
objective: implement-media-discovery
value: Eliminates opaque hand-written WebSocket calls for media automation and agent planning.
impact: Adds current media browsing and search coverage with bounded machine contracts.
outcome: Production-ready CLI commands merged with exact-head checks and zero unresolved reviews.
why_now: Home Assistant current development exposes searchable media sources that are absent from the typed CLI.
parent: hac-ln1v
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 96
sprint: 2026-07-media-discovery
release: 2026.7.26
